Enhancement: Add reusable Trivy vulnerability scan workflow

App repositories and core can now scan their built distribution tree for known
HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerabilities, failing the job when a fix is available. The scan
runs `trivy rootfs` over the unpacked tree rather than `trivy fs` over the
checkout: the fs scanner does not enable Trivy's gobinary analyzer, which is how
a Go 1.22.4 rclone carrying 48 HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs shipped unnoticed inside
migrate_to_ocis, and Trivy does not look inside the .tar.gz either. A missing
distribution tree fails the job instead of scanning nothing and reporting clean.

https://github.com/owncloud/reusable-workflows/pull/92
